From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:06:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/48] net: airoha: xpon: do not arm TO1 in O2

G.984.3 uses TO1 to bound the serial-number and ranging states; in O2
the ONU waits for Upstream_Overhead with no timeout. gpon_cb_state_changed()
fell through from O2 into the O3/O4 case and armed TO1 there as well.
The expiry handler ignores O2, so this was harmless, but it queued a
pointless work every 10 s while the ONU sat in O2.

The stock driver (gpon_act_change_gpon_state) arms the TO1 timer on
entering O3 and on entering O4, and not in O2. Do the same: cancel TO1
in O2 and keep the restart on O3 and O4 entry.

No change to when activation times out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 0335521..a9ed3da 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -2836,10 +2836,16 @@ static void gpon_cb_state_changed(void *hw_priv, enum gpon_state state)
 		priv->bit_delay = 0;
 		gpon_set_bit_delay(priv, 0);
 		priv->psync_sof_o5 = U32_MAX;
-		fallthrough;
+		/*
+		 * TO1 limits the serial-number and ranging states; O2 waits
+		 * for Upstream_Overhead without a timeout. The stock driver
+		 * arms TO1 only on entering O3 and O4.
+		 */
+		cancel_delayed_work(&priv->to1_work);
+		break;
 	case GPON_O3_SERIAL_NUMBER:
 	case GPON_O4_RANGING:
-		/* Start / restart TO1 timer */
+		/* Start / restart TO1, as the stock driver does in O3 and O4. */
 		mod_delayed_work(priv->fsm_wq, &priv->to1_work,
 				 msecs_to_jiffies(GPON_TO1_MS));
 		break;
